WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.390
A seedling bends to the light.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.920
A student measures the angle
of the bend five times.

3
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:11.770
28, 29, 28, 29, 28 degrees.

4
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.160
The readings barely differ at all.

5
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:18.930
Then a later check reveals
the true angle: 35 degrees.

6
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.710
Every reading was off.

7
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.640
So how can readings that
agree so well all be wrong?

8
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.500
In this mission, you'll
compare four targets,

9
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:31.950
each hit in a very different pattern,
and learn what each pattern tells you.

10
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.290
Then you'll spot the
weak points of a method,

11
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.940
and match each problem to
the fix that actually works.

12
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: explain how five readings
can agree perfectly and still all be wrong.
